{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Pm25n6L3q55MoQMZyFSQp1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a personal productivity / R&D mission-control system built for J.C. Liechty. Grounded claims from the project's own docs:\n\n**Purpose**\n- A single-folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), plain-markdown-as-source-of-truth task and project manager â€” DASHBOARD/PROJECTS/INBOX plus per-domain files (academic, commercial, family, writing). No database, no syncing.\n- It has grown a second mission: a **\"mission control\" for trio-driven R&D**, where each project's research â†’ plan â†’ build work (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) is tracked as durable, summarized history.\n\n**What it does**\n- Runs as a persistent local web server (`anchor_gui.py`) bound to `http://localhost:8777`, owned by the NSSM Windows service `anchor`; it reads/writes the markdown files directly via a local HTTP API and regenerates the dashboard HTML on every request.\n- Supports the full task lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored) from either the browser GUI or a mirrored CLI (`anchor.py`).\n- Self-tests daily at 5 AM (`anchor_healthcheck.py` via Task Scheduler): parses every file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint and the v2 + v3 R&D surfaces fully stubbed, and writes `health_reports/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.\n- **R&D v2 surface:** sessions (one trio run = one session), cached/validated summaries, first-class imported history, folder reconcile, a \"Grass Catchers\" idea lane, deliverable declare/pin, and an interactive terminal substrate (stream-json REPL).\n- **R&D v3 \"Mission Control\":** real ConPTY terminals (the one permitted native dep, optional `pywinpty`), per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry, a stacking window manager, thin project rows with proactive cached summaries, in-place expandable session summaries, stage handoffs, a runnable deliverable preview (HARD-guarded off port 8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n\n**What it ships**\n- The declared deliverable is **`anchor_gui.py`** â€” the self-contained, Python-stdlib-only web app (the v3 terminal subsystem's `pywinpty` is the single declared, optional, lazily-imported exception, enforced by `distro.py`'s import scan).\n- Supporting modules: the CLI engine (`anchor.py`), the healthcheck, and the v2/v3 R&D modules (`sessions.py`, `summarizer.py`, `pty_manager.py`, `session_registry.py`, `worktrees.py`, `terminal_session.py`, `handoff.py`, `preview_server.py`, etc.), plus frozen design/plan docs under `planning/rnd-v2/` and `planning/rnd-v3/`.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: per memory, v3 was **built by Foreman (all 10 waves green) but is on branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v3` and not yet merged/deployed** â€” though the working tree here shows v3 artifacts present, so the merge state is worth confirming if it matters."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20212,"cache_read_input_tokens":20573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20212},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df6da251-0c72-4723-a27a-051fc265d129","uuid":"c148c639-fe30-4a56-8943-24ef27741bab","request_id":"req_011CbyRB8fPyuBHgQYj7GqZS"}
